## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

**Framework:** MSTest · **Tests:** 10 · **Production:** `ProductCatalog.cs` (10 public members)

---

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| 🔴 Critical | 2 (systemic — affects all 10 tests) |
| 🟡 Medium | 1 |
| Total | 3 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test class. Every public method on `ProductCatalog` is called exactly once, achieving high line coverage, but almost nothing is verified. Six tests have **zero assertions**; the remaining four assert only `IsNotNull`, which can never fail for the types returned. These tests will pass even if every method is broken.

---

### 🔴 Critical #1 — Coverage Touching (Systematic)

All 10 tests follow the same pattern: call a method, discard or null-check the result. The class walks the entire public API in declaration order with no real verification. This inflates coverage to ~95% while proving nothing.

**Affected:** Every test in the file.

---

### 🔴 Critical #2 — No Assertions / Trivially-True Assertions

**6 tests with zero assertions:**

| Test | Line | What it misses |
|------|------|----------------|
| `AddProduct_Works` | 17 | Never verifies the product was stored |
| `UpdatePrice_Works` | 32 | Never verifies the price changed |
| `RemoveProduct_Works` | 39 | Never verifies the product was deleted |
| `GetProductCount_Works` | 64 | Never asserts the count value |
| `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` | 69 | Never verifies prices were reduced |
| `ImportFromCsv_Works` | 85 | Never verifies products were imported |

**4 tests with only `Assert.IsNotNull` (trivially true):**

`GetProduct`, `Search`, `GetAll` return `Product?`/`List<Product>` — the list variants can never be null (they return `new List` or `.ToList()`), so `IsNotNull` is always-true. `GetProduct` could return null for a *missing* SKU, but the test adds the product first, so it's trivially non-null.

| Test | Line | What it misses |
|------|------|----------------|
| `GetProduct_Works` | 28 | Never checks Sku/Name/Price of returned product |
| `SearchProducts_Works` | 51 | Never checks result count or content |
| `GetAllProducts_Works` | 59 | Never checks the list has the expected item |
| `ExportToCsv_Works` | 81 | Never checks CSV content |

**Concrete fixes (before → after):**

```csharp
// AddProduct_Works → AddProduct_StoresProduct
[TestMethod]
public void AddProduct_StoresProduct()
{
    var product = new Product("SKU-001", "Widget", 9.99m);
    _catalog.AddProduct(product);

    var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
    Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved?.Name);
    Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved?.Price);
}

